$DIR/main.p:8:2: packed field h is an array of uint16, whose elements are 2 bytes wide, in a big-endian packed type
    A big-endian packed type cannot have an array field whose elements are wider
    than one byte, whatever its backing. The spec gives no order for the bytes
    of such elements in big-endian storage. An array of single bytes, such as
    [4]byte or [2]uint8, is allowed, and so is a reserved _ field.
    Declare one field for each element instead, or use an array of bytes and put
    the values together yourself.
    (see "packed types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.14)
    (run "pluto explain E2111" for a longer explanation)

